    {
      "title": "Bellwork",
      "backgroundImageUrl": "https://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&id=1xwZJfyO-LDc4RKMrTNpXBEOYU-TW86M4",
      "bullets": [
        "Think about the last time you filled out an online form on your phone versus your computer.",
        "What made the experience easy or frustrating?",
        "What are 3 features that make a form user-friendly on both desktop and mobile devices?"
      ],
      "layout": "title_and_bullets",
      "imageUrl": "",
      "imagePosition": "right",
      "speakerNotes": "Time Estimate: 5 minutes\nTeacher: Have students reflect on their personal experiences with forms across devices. This connects to responsive design principles we'll cover today. Call on students to share their thoughts and relate their answers to concepts like touch targets, readability, and ease of navigation.\nStudents: Reflect and write responses in their note-taker, then share when called upon."
    },
    {
      "title": "Today's Objectives",
